<concept id="t00300">
	<title id="e02280">Operating rear fog lamp</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>lighting 
					<indexterm>operating rear fog lamp</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
				<indexterm>operating rear fog lamp</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e02281">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e02282">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OSW035467L.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e02283"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<ul id="e02284">
			<li>
				<p>To turn on the rear fog lamp, turn the rear fog lamp switch (1) to the <term translate="no">ON</term> position with the headlights turned on.</p>
				<p>The rear fog lamp also turn on when the rear fog lamp switch is turned on after the headlight switch is in the position lamp (<image href="../../images/WKIA_049.eps" align="left" scale="15" placement="inline" outputclass="nolabel" id="e02285"/>) position.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>To turn off the rear fog lamp, turn the rear fog light switch to the <term translate="no">ON</term> position again.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</conbody>
</concept>